course: dictionary
lesson: 2021
title: Confess: owning up to the truth
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To confess means to admit something you did wrong, or something you feel ashamed of. When you confess, you stop hiding the truth. «Mason-Tyler breaks the TV remote and his big brother takes the blame, but Mason-Tyler feels so bad that he confesses.» The clue is the feeling: he feels bad, so he tells the truth.
explain: Look at the words around confess to find its meaning. «I must confess I love cold pizza» is different. Here confess just means admit, and nobody has done anything wrong. Ask yourself: is this about a wrong, or about a small thing I am owning up to? Then try admit in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Confess also has special meanings in some places. In church, people confess their sins to God, or to a priest. In law, to confess a crime means to tell the police or a court that you did it. The words near confess show which meaning is in use: confess your sins, confess to a crime, confess everything.
explain: Being honest early usually makes things better than being caught. «People who have confessed can slip again; forgiveness does not run out, but each wrong must be put right.» Owning up is the first step, and making things right is the next.
fact: Confess means to admit that you did something wrong or something you are ashamed of.
fact: «I must confess» can just mean I admit, as in «I must confess I love cold pizza».
fact: To confess a crime means to tell the police or a court that you did it.
fact: Phrases with confess include confess to something, confess your sins, and confess everything.
fact: In a story, a character who confesses brings the truth into the open, so the reader learns the answer to the mystery.
exercise: «In Ohio, Mason-Tyler breaks the TV remote and his big brother takes the blame, but Mason-Tyler feels so bad that he confesses.» What does confesses mean here? | Hides the remote under his bed | Breaks something else | *Admits the truth about what he did | Blames his brother even more
exercise: Ayla says, «I must confess I love cold pizza.» Is she admitting a crime? | *No, it is a small thing she is admitting | Yes, she has told the police | No, she is asking for help | Yes, she did a crime at lunch
exercise: Which word means the same as confess in its everyday sense? | Forget | Shout | Hide | *Admit
test: «Whoever conceals their sins does not prosper, but the one who confesses and renounces them finds mercy.» In this sentence, what does conceals mean? | Forgives | Counts | *Hides | Admits
test: «Scripture asks for both: confess the wrong and make it good.» What two things does this sentence ask for? | Count the sins and pray | Hide the wrong and forget it | *Confess the wrong and make it good | Confess only to a priest
exam: A friend says, «I must confess I broke your pencil.» What does confess mean in this sentence? | Hides | Shouts | Breaks | *Admits
